==English==

===Etymology===
* From the Hebrew word [[הר מגידו]] (''har megiddo''), used in [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_%28World_English%29/Revelation#Chapter_16 Revelation 16:16], referring to Mount [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Megiddo Megiddo], "''the place of the last battle at the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_Judgment Day of Judgment]''".

===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɛdən|-ɛdən]]

===Hyphenation===
Ar·ma·ged·don

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

#{{Christianity}} The place where the final battle will be fought between the forces of [[good]] and [[evil]].
#{{Christianity}} The final conflict between good and evil.
# Any great and crucial conflict.

